increasePositionSize.t.sol
├── when caller is not the position owner
│   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__NOT_POSITION_OWNER} error
└── when caller is the position owner
    ├── when position is already closed
    │   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__POSITION_ALREADY_CLOSED} error
    └── when position is open
        ├── when new size is less than or equal to current size
        │   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__INVALID_POSITION_SIZE} error
        └── when new size is greater than current size
            ├── when current collateral is less than computed position fee for size delta
            │   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__INSUFFICIENT_COLLATERAL} error
            └── when current collateral is greater than or equal to computed position fee for size delta
                ├── when resulting position is liquidatable
                │   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__LIQUIDATABLE_POSITION} error
                └── when resulting position is not liquidatable
                    ├── it should update position size
                    ├── it should decrease position collateral by computed position fee
                    ├── it should increase position size in tokens by computed size delta in tokens
                    ├── it should increase total open interest for token and side
                    ├── it should emit the {PositionSizeIncreased} event
                    ├── it should call {reserveAssets} on pool with expected reserve amount for size delta
                    └── it should transfer the computed position fee from perpex to pool
